#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:9
msgid "Use Slidev for the PyCon JP 2026 talk slide deck"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:11
msgid "Context and Problem Statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:13
msgid ""
"pyvista-wasm was accepted as a talk at PyCon JP 2026 — [\"PyVista on "
"WebAssembly: "
"サーバーレス3D可視化の実現\"](https://pretalx.com/pyconjp2026/talk/review/VVJZFPCFCJCRGGKWEWKPYC3QXF8YE3A9)."
" The talk must demonstrate PyVista running live in the browser via "
"WebAssembly, walk the audience through the TypeScript-glue architecture, "
"and show Python/TypeScript code snippets with syntax highlighting. We "
"need to pick a slide tool that lets us embed those live browser demos "
"directly in the deck, keeps the source version-controllable alongside the"
" rest of the repository, and is easy to author and review through the "
"normal PR flow. Which slide tool should we adopt for this talk?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:15
msgid "Decision Drivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:17
msgid ""
"**Live web demo embedding**: The talk's centerpiece is a live, in-browser"
" PyVista WASM demo. The slide tool must be able to run or embed that demo"
" inside a slide without leaving the presentation context. This is a "
"knock-out criterion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:18
msgid ""
"**Code syntax highlighting**: The deck shows Python and TypeScript code; "
"first-class syntax highlighting with line highlighting and code "
"animations is essential for a technical audience."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:19
msgid ""
"**Version-control friendliness**: Slide source must be plain text that "
"diffs and reviews well in Git, so the deck can travel through the same PR"
" flow as code (see [ADR-0000](0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-"
"records.md))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:20
msgid ""
"**Ease of authoring**: The deck must be authorable efficiently with hot-"
"reload preview, so iteration is fast before the talk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:21
msgid ""
"**Portability**: The deck should be presentable offline, exportable to "
"PDF for sharing, and deployable as a static site."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:22
msgid ""
"**Community adoption**: Prefer a tool with an active community, "
"documentation, and a healthy ecosystem to reduce risk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:24
msgid "Considered Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:26
msgid ""
"[Slidev](https://sli.dev/) — Vue-powered presentation framework for "
"developers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:27
msgid ""
"[sphinx-revealjs](https://github.com/attakei/sphinx-revealjs) — Sphinx "
"extension to build reveal.js presentations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:28
msgid "[reveal.js](https://revealjs.com/) — The HTML presentation framework"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:29
msgid "[Marp](https://marp.app/) — Markdown presentation ecosystem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:30
#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:108
msgid "Google Slides — Cloud-based WYSIWYG presentation tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:31
#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:117
msgid "Microsoft PowerPoint — Desktop WYSIWYG presentation tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:32
msgid ""
"[JupyterLab Slides / RISE](https://rise.readthedocs.io/) — Live Jupyter "
"notebook slideshow extension"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:34
msgid "Decision Outcome"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:36
msgid ""
"Chosen option: \"Slidev\", because it is the only option that satisfies "
"the knock-out criterion — embedding live web demos — *and* provides best-"
"in-class code highlighting, Markdown-based version-controllable "
"authoring, and a developer-friendly authoring experience. Slidev is a "
"Vue-based single-page application, so the PyVista WASM demo can be "
"embedded as a live Vue component or iframe and run directly inside a "
"slide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:38
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:40
msgid ""
"Good, because live PyVista WASM demos can run inside slides via Vue "
"components or iframes, making the talk fully interactive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:41
msgid ""
"Good, because slides are authored in Markdown, diffing cleanly in Git and"
" travelling through the same PR review flow as the rest of the "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:42
msgid ""
"Good, because Slidev's Shiki-based syntax highlighting supports line "
"highlighting, code animations, and code blocks with Monaco editor "
"integration — ideal for a technical talk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:43
msgid ""
"Good, because Slidev exports to PDF, PNG, and a standalone SPA, giving us"
" portable fallbacks for offline presenting and sharing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:44
msgid ""
"Good, because the deck can be deployed as a static site (e.g. on GitHub "
"Pages) alongside the project documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:45
msgid ""
"Bad, because Slidev requires a Node.js toolchain, adding a build "
"dependency that the Python-only parts of the project do not need."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:46
msgid ""
"Bad, because Slidev's community, while active, is smaller than "
"reveal.js's or Google Slides's, so fewer third-party themes and "
"integrations are available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:47
msgid ""
"Neutral, because the deck will live in the repository under version "
"control, which is the desired outcome but does require maintaining slide "
"source alongside code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:49
msgid "Confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:51
msgid "Compliance with this decision will be confirmed by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:53
msgid ""
"A Slidev project is initialised in the repository (e.g. under a `slides/`"
" directory) with a `slides.md` entry point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:54
msgid ""
"At least one slide embeds a live PyVista WASM demo (via Vue component or "
"iframe) that renders a 3D plot in the browser during the presentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:55
msgid ""
"The deck is reviewable through a PR linked to issue "
"[#278](https://github.com/tkoyama010/pyvista-wasm/issues/278)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:56
msgid "The deck exports successfully to PDF for offline sharing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:58
msgid "Pros and Cons of the Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:60
msgid "Slidev — Vue-powered presentation framework for developers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:62
msgid "See [https://sli.dev/](https://sli.dev/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:64
msgid ""
"Good, because it is a Vue/Vite-based SPA, so live web demos — the knock-"
"out criterion — can be embedded as native Vue components or iframes and "
"run inside a slide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:65
msgid ""
"Good, because it uses Shiki for syntax highlighting with support for line"
" highlighting, diff lines, and code animations, which is ideal for "
"showing Python and TypeScript code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:66
msgid ""
"Good, because slides are authored in Markdown with YAML frontmatter per "
"slide, satisfying the version-control-friendliness driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:67
msgid ""
"Good, because it ships a hot-reload dev server (`slidev dev`) for fast "
"authoring iteration, satisfying the ease-of-authoring driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:68
msgid ""
"Good, because it exports to PDF, PNG, and a standalone SPA, satisfying "
"the portability driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:69
msgid ""
"Neutral, because it requires a Node.js toolchain, which is a new build "
"dependency for this predominantly Python project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:70
msgid ""
"Neutral, because its community (~40k GitHub stars) is active and growing "
"but smaller than reveal.js's."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:72
msgid "sphinx-revealjs — Sphinx extension to build reveal.js presentations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:74
msgid ""
"See [https://github.com/attakei/sphinx-"
"revealjs](https://github.com/attakei/sphinx-revealjs)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:76
msgid ""
"Good, because it reuses the project's existing Sphinx toolchain "
"(`docs/conf.py` already configures Sphinx + MyST parser), requiring no "
"new build dependency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:77
msgid ""
"Good, because slides are authored in reStructuredText or MyST Markdown, "
"which is already enabled in this project, satisfying the version-control-"
"friendliness driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:78
msgid ""
"Good, because it stays within the Python ecosystem, consistent with a "
"predominantly Python project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:79
msgid ""
"Good, because the maintainer is a Japanese developer active in the PyCon "
"JP community, offering natural community alignment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:80
msgid ""
"Neutral, because it wraps reveal.js, so live demo embedding is iframe-"
"based — functional but less seamless than Slidev's native Vue component "
"model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:81
msgid ""
"Neutral, because code syntax highlighting relies on reveal.js's "
"highlight.js, which lacks Slidev's Shiki features (line highlighting, "
"code animations, Monaco integration)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:82
msgid ""
"Bad, because its community (~129 GitHub stars) is significantly smaller "
"than Slidev's or reveal.js's, meaning fewer third-party themes and less "
"community support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:83
msgid ""
"Bad, because it lacks a dedicated hot-reload dev server comparable to "
"Slidev's `slidev dev` (only `sphinx-autobuild` is available, which is "
"less tailored to slideshow authoring)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:85
msgid "reveal.js — The HTML presentation framework"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:87
msgid "See [https://revealjs.com/](https://revealjs.com/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:89
msgid ""
"Good, because it can embed live web demos via iframes and custom HTML, "
"partially satisfying the knock-out criterion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:90
msgid "Good, because it has built-in syntax highlighting via highlight.js."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:91
msgid ""
"Good, because it has the largest community (~68k GitHub stars) and a "
"long, proven track record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:92
msgid ""
"Good, because it is an HTML/JS framework that deploys as a static site, "
"satisfying portability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:93
msgid ""
"Neutral, because while a Markdown plugin exists, authoring is primarily "
"HTML-based, which is more verbose than Markdown-first tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:94
msgid ""
"Bad, because embedding live Vue components is not native — iframes are "
"the main mechanism, which is less seamless than Slidev's component model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:95
msgid ""
"Bad, because the HTML-centric authoring flow is less ergonomic for a "
"Markdown-heavy project than Slidev or Marp."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:97
msgid "Marp — Markdown presentation ecosystem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:99
msgid "See [https://marp.app/](https://marp.app/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:101
msgid ""
"Good, because it is pure Markdown, maximally satisfying the version-"
"control-friendliness and ease-of-authoring drivers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:102
msgid "Good, because it exports to PDF, PPTX, and HTML, satisfying portability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:103
msgid ""
"Good, because it has built-in syntax highlighting and a clean, minimal "
"authoring experience."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:104
msgid ""
"Neutral, because it is primarily a Markdown-to-slide *converter*, not an "
"interactive runtime — live demos must be embedded as iframes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:105
msgid ""
"Bad, because it cannot run live Vue components or interactive web content"
" natively, making the live-demo embedding less seamless than Slidev."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:106
msgid ""
"Bad, because it lacks presenter features like code animations and live "
"component rendering that a technical talk benefits from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:110
msgid ""
"Good, because it is extremely easy to author with a WYSIWYG editor and "
"requires no toolchain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:111
msgid ""
"Good, because it has massive general adoption and seamless cloud "
"collaboration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:112
msgid ""
"Neutral, because it can embed external content via \"Insert > Embed "
"link,\" but support is limited and not designed for live code execution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:113
msgid ""
"Bad, because it has no native code syntax highlighting, requiring "
"workarounds like images or third-party add-ons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:114
msgid ""
"Bad, because slide source is a binary cloud document, failing the "
"version-control-friendliness driver — the deck cannot be reviewed in a "
"PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:115
msgid ""
"Bad, because embedding a live, interactive WASM demo is unreliable and "
"constrained by the embed sandbox."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:119
msgid "Good, because it is widely adopted and familiar to a general audience."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:120
msgid "Good, because it exports to PDF and runs offline, satisfying portability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:121
msgid ""
"Neutral, because it supports web add-ins, but these are heavyweight and "
"not designed for live WASM demos."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:122
msgid "Bad, because it has no native code syntax highlighting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:123
msgid ""
"Bad, because slide source is a binary `.pptx` file, failing the version-"
"control-friendliness driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:124
msgid ""
"Bad, because embedding live, interactive browser content is severely "
"limited."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:126
msgid "JupyterLab Slides / RISE — Live Jupyter notebook slideshow extension"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:128
msgid "See [https://rise.readthedocs.io/](https://rise.readthedocs.io/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:130
msgid ""
"Good, because it can execute live Python code in notebook cells during "
"the presentation, which is appealing for a Python audience."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:131
msgid "Good, because notebook code cells have syntax highlighting built in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:132
msgid ""
"Neutral, because notebooks are JSON and can be version-controlled, but "
"diffs are noisy when outputs are saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:133
msgid ""
"Bad, because embedding a live, in-browser *WASM application* inside a "
"Jupyter slideshow is awkward — the WASM demo is a web app, not a notebook"
" cell, so it would need an iframe workaround."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:134
msgid ""
"Bad, because RISE is less actively maintained and has a smaller community"
" than the other developer-oriented options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0001-use-slidev-for-pycon-jp-2026-talk-slides.md:135
msgid ""
"Bad, because the slideshow UX (navigation, transitions, layout control) "
"is more limited than purpose-built slide frameworks."
msgstr ""

